Part Two

Rights of Children Article 6 (1)Every Child has the right to:
a. live, grow, develop, and participate reasonably in accordance with human dignity and dignity, and receive protection from violence and discrimination;
b. obtain a name as personal identity and citizenship status; c. worship according to their religion, think, and express themselves in accordance with the level of intelligence and age under the guidance of Parents or Guardians; d. obtain education and teaching in the context of personal development and level of intelligence in accordance with interests and talents and receive protection in educational units from sexual crimes and Violence committed by educators, education personnel, fellow students, and/or other parties;
e. obtain protection from being the target of persecution, torture, or imposition of inhuman punishment;
f. obtain freedom in accordance with the law and arrest, detention, or criminal imprisonment of Children shall only be carried out if in accordance with applicable law and can only be carried out as a last resort;
g. be cared for by their own Parents, unless there are reasons and/or valid legal rules showing that the separation is in the best interests of the Child and is a last consideration;
h. obtain protection from abuse in political activities, involvement in armed conflicts, involvement in social unrest, involvement in events containing elements of Violence, involvement in warfare and, sexual crimes;
i. participate, express opinions and think in accordance with conscience and religion;

j. receive oral or written information in accordance with the age stage and development of the Child;
k. associate and assemble; and
l. rest, play, recreate, create, and engage in cultural arts, obtain play facilities that meet health and safety requirements and are adapted to the age of the Child, the ability level of the Child, and the environment so as not to hinder and disturb. (2)Every child who is deprived of liberty has the right to:

a.be treated humanely;

b.placement separated from adults;

c.obtain legal assistance or other assistance effectively at every stage of applicable legal remedies; and

d.defend themselves and obtain justice before an objective and impartial Juvenile Court in a closed session to the public. (3)Every child who is a victim or perpetrator of sexual violence or who is in conflict with the law has the right to confidentiality.

4. Every Child with Disabilities in addition to obtaining rights as referred to in paragraph (1) is also entitled to obtain:

a.special education/special education;

b.rehabilitation;
c. social assistance; and

d.maintenance of social welfare standards.

5. Every Child who has excellence has the right to receive special education.

